{"tag":"QQ9E","kind":"definition","paper":"1006.4617","version":"1","local":"definition-1","file":"","number":"2.1","section":"sec-2","order":1,"title":"Definition","body_md":"\\begin{equation}  w(G,{\\cal{T}}) =  \\int_0^1 \\prod_{\\ell \\in {\\cal{T}}} dw_\\ell   \n\\prod_{\\ell \\not\\in {\\cal{T}}} x^{\\cal{T}}_{\\ell}(\\{w\\})\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $x^{\\cal{T}}_{\\ell}(\\{w\\})$ is the infimum over the $w_{\\ell'}$ parameters \nover the lines $\\ell'$ forming the {\\it unique} path in ${\\cal{T}}$ joining the ends of $\\ell$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"definition","item":"definition","head":"environment","counter":"definition","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Treeslmp.tex","from":172,"to":178},"hash":"sha256:6e4ed9c06aa0676b9a19023aa5a47d671b5c86dcd253223daed4edc6492af096","minhash":"","census":"1006.4617v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.23"}
{"tag":"W35W","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1006.4617","version":"1","local":"lemma-1","file":"","label":"bary","number":"2.1","section":"sec-2","order":2,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"The relation\n\\begin{equation}  \\sum_{{\\cal{F}}\\subset G}  w(G,{\\cal{F}}) =1  \\label{bary}\n\\end{equation}\nholds for any connected graph $G$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"counter","labels":["bary"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"here","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Treeslmp.tex","from":179,"to":183},"hash":"sha256:68c461e7fe650840c5c471668701f187f0e60a74d1105b8ee94b8b2ac8476ef1","minhash":"","census":"1006.4617v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.23"}
{"tag":"Z2V4","kind":"proof","paper":"1006.4617","version":"1","local":"head-1","file":"","section":"sec-2","order":3,"title":"Proof","body_md":"It is a simple consequence of the forest formula \\cite{BK,AR1} applied to \nthe lines of the graph $G$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"head","item":"proof","head":"manual","scope":"paper","proves":"lemma-1","attach":3,"span":{"file":"Treeslmp.tex","from":184,"to":187},"hash":"sha256:edf5b8fbd231d26c4364c58bd105fdb89a0e473a18830e818c506d064895aff0","minhash":"","census":"1006.4617v1#proof-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.23"}
{"tag":"T5YR","kind":"definition","paper":"1006.4617","version":"1","local":"definition-2","file":"","number":"4.1","section":"sec-6","order":4,"title":"Definition","body_md":"We define the collapse $\\bar G'$ of such a $G'$ graph as\nthe graph obtained by contracting each cycle to a \"bold\" vertex (see Figure 5).\nWe write $\\bar G' {\\ \\rm coll\\ } G'$ if $\\bar G'$ is the collapse of $G'$, and define\nthe amplitude of the collapsed graph $ \\bar G'$ as equal to that of $G'$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"definition","item":"definition","head":"environment","counter":"definition","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Treeslmp.tex","from":403,"to":408},"hash":"sha256:c8c1a8aa3351886f6e4f31c311d7a7ee2d03673fbcc76a6cb69ecda992b96b9e","minhash":"","census":"1006.4617v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.23"}
{"tag":"0TXH","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"1006.4617","version":"1","local":"theorem-1","file":"","number":"4.1","section":"sec-6","order":5,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"For $\\lambda$ small \n\\begin{equation}  \\sum_{\\bar {\\cal{T}}}  \\vert A_{\\bar {\\cal{T}}} \\vert \u003c \\infty\n\\end{equation}\nthe result being the {\\it Borel sum} of the initial perturbative series \\cite{R2}.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","proof_status":"cited","origin":"cited","span":{"file":"Treeslmp.tex","from":432,"to":436},"hash":"sha256:09f90f7b8cf7705fa9eef5a71c375f9127a96c0a074f4e723c6094c36357435d","minhash":"","census":"1006.4617v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.23"}
{"tag":"RENV","kind":"remark","subkind":"example","paper":"1006.4617","version":"1","local":"example-1","file":"","label":"contracexample","number":"5.1","section":"sec-7","order":6,"title":"Example","body_md":"\\begin{figure}[!htb]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[scale=0.60]{contracexample.pdf}\n\\caption{The example of '123' contractions.}\n\\label{contracexample}\n\\end{figure} \nWe consider the $123$ case for example. This is shown more explicitly in Figure(\\ref{contracexample}). We use $a, b,\\cdots, f$ to label the $\\sigma$ fields attached to the  vertices. After the Wick contractions we get three different graphs $A$, $B$ and $C$. The number of possibilities to get $A$ is $3$, the number to get $B$ is $2\\times 3=6$ and the number to get $C$ is also 6. So the relative weight for graph $A$ is $3/(3+6+6)=1/5$ and the relative weights for $B$ and $C$ are both $6/(3+6+6)=2/5$. As we could read directly from the loop vertex formula that the total number of $123$ contraction graphs is $960$, we get finally the combinatoric factor of graph $A$ to be $960\\times 1/5=192$, and the corresponding factors for graphs $B$ and $C$ are $960\\times 2/5=384$. This result agrees with the one coming from the Feynman graph computation.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"example","item":"example","head":"environment","counter":"example","number_from":"counter","labels":["contracexample"],"scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Treeslmp.tex","from":521,"to":529},"hash":"sha256:df23e2461b4b2ab70bb6f0a90d79df354a98dcc70ebcfc00c845e5eb6fa1b3ae","minhash":"","census":"1006.4617v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.23"}
{"tag":"I5JQ","kind":"problem","subkind":"conjecture","paper":"1006.4617","version":"1","local":"conjecture-1","file":"","number":"6.1","section":"sec-8","order":7,"title":"Conjecture","body_md":"For $\\lambda$ small \n\\begin{equation}  \\sum_{\\bar {\\cal{T}}}  \\vert A_{D,\\bar {\\cal{T}}} \\vert \u003c \\infty\n\\end{equation}\nthe result being the Borel sum of the initial perturbative series.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"conjecture","item":"conjecture","head":"environment","counter":"conjecture","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Treeslmp.tex","from":554,"to":558},"hash":"sha256:0d99ed2cf5071cef5d039e72131b3ca6361b99b38089ad5cfa8635f3784b7348","minhash":"","census":"1006.4617v1#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.23"}
